      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(2,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X\\le 2.4)=0.5987,$ find $\\sigma .$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5596\\,$ | $\\,0.5636\\,$ | $\\,0.5675\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5987\\,$ | $\\,0.6026\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6368\\,$ | $\\,0.6406\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2.4) & =0.5987 \\\\ P(Z\\le \\frac{2.4-2}{\\sigma }) & =0.5987 \\\\ Φ(\\frac{0.4}{\\sigma }) & =0.5987 \\\\ \\frac{0.4}{\\sigma } & ={Φ}^{-1}(0.5987)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(0.25)=0.5987\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(0.5987)=0.25.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.4}{\\sigma } & =0.25 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{0.4}{0.25} \\\\ \\sigma  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
